{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed. Gerrit change 1951 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1951) received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero unresolved comments and is MERGED to main as of 2026-08-20T06:49:53Z; commit 6451d3ff02 carries the rebar-ticket: baeb-4f4b-3227-457e trailer and the DCO sign-off. CI's Verified +1 ran the whole tree on the merged commit, which is the authoritative signal for this close; no local full-suite re-run was used as a gate. All seven acceptance criteria are met and ticked: the slow-progress sentinel still dribbles above the floor across a full injected 1s low-speed window and still fails only for a non-stall reason; the ACLI read sentinel still launches exactly _MAX_ATTEMPTS real child sessions and polls every recorded PID to absence; production timeout/stall/grace/drain defaults are byte-unchanged (120s/3s/2s call/grace/drain and a 10s low-speed window); both files retain real subprocess and real loopback-socket execution and now complete in 6.13s together (down from 12.67s); the single upper-bound wall-clock assertion was left at its 10s ceiling rather than tightened, and scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py reports clean; every reap assertion that depends on child-side setup is now ordered by an explicit readiness gate; and each touched sentinel was shown RED under a seeded defect and GREEN after revert (ten seeds, detailed in the preceding comment)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787208696876957001,"uuid":"92bfd403-ae61-4315-b385-548957ddde65"}